{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792486689,"nonce":"iL1ygaG7w+LNanVhRBtT7gGXLZg=","title":"Render Markdown HTML and release inactive preview images","message":"The production preview shows raw HTML in RayDE's README rather than the intended centered logo, headings and sized images. File menus also repeat the Markdown type in their Preview label. Inactive preview tabs keep their mounted controls and decoded image data.\n\nRender document HTML through an HTML5 parser and Ashui components, including image dimensions/alignment, inline formatting, links, tables and native details/summary. Keep executable/browser-only content out of the document tree. Use Open Preview in file menus while retaining the command palette's Markdown qualification.\n\nMake Markdown render resources follow the visible tab/root: release raster pixels, document SVGs, code viewers and CanvasKit views while inactive, preserve the compact document model, and restore on selection. Downsample raster decode buffers to the displayed dimensions with backing-resolution allowance and a bounded maximum. Verify actual bitmap-disposal callbacks across multiple image previews and repeated tab switches.\n\nAshui's 2D ImageAtlas currently uses Rgba8unorm and display-size rasterization; its block-compression path is for 3D mesh textures. No claim of BC-compressed UI textures is made by the raster downsampling change.","files":null}]}